# ExileCrafting craft scripts

A `.csx` here is not a normal C# file. It is a Roslyn script compiled with `CraftContext` as its
globals object, running top to bottom with no class and no namespace, driving the real mouse
against Path of Exile 1.

Read `slop/reference/scripting-api.md` before writing one, and
`slop/reference/script-authoring.md` for the shape and the worked examples. The imports and the
awaiting rule are not guessable from the code.

## Hard rules

- Only `await` a `ctx.*` call. `Task.Delay`, `.Result`, `.Wait()` and `Task.Run` break the run
  with "called off the main thread" or "already has an operation in flight". There is no sleep;
  to wait, loop on a `ctx` call.
- Currency names are exact `BaseItemTypes.BaseName` strings, ordinal and case-sensitive:
  `"Orb of Alteration"`. They live in `ExileCrafting/data/currency.txt`. Harvest craft text lives
  in `ExileCrafting/data/harvest-crafts.txt` and must filter to exactly one row.
- `ApplyCurrencyUntil` / `ApplyPairUntil` conditions are synchronous. `ctx.CountMods` inside
  them; `ctx.CheckMods` and `ctx.Ask` both throw there.
- `ctx.Item` reads memory on every access. Never cache it; re-invoke it inside lambdas.
- Never catch `CraftGuardException` or `OperationCanceledException`. They are the run limits and
  the abort hotkey working.
- Prefer `ApplyCurrencyUntil` over a `while` loop of `ApplyCurrency`. One pickup instead of a
  trip back to the stash per orb.
- Available imports are only: `System`, `System.Linq`, `System.Threading.Tasks`, `ExileCrafting`,
  `ExileCore.PoEMemory.Components`, `ExileCore.Shared.Enums`,
  `ExileCore.PoEMemory.MemoryObjects`, `ExileCore.PoEMemory.Models`, `ItemFilterLibrary`.
- `ctx.ApplyHarvest` needs `// Type: Harvest` in the header block.

## Header

```csharp
// Name: <what it is>
// Description: <one line>
// Type: Currency
```

Only the leading comment block is parsed. `Type` is `Currency` or `Harvest`.

## Shape

Read the item, choose the single action that moves this state forward, apply it, loop. Guard on
`ctx.Item.IsEmpty`, on the expected `BaseName`, and on `ItemRarity.Unique` first. Every action
returns `false` when it could not complete - check it and break, the craft log already says why.

```csharp
while (true)
{
    if (ctx.Item.IsEmpty) { ctx.Log("crafting slot is empty"); break; }
    if (ctx.Item.BaseName != "Large Cluster Jewel") { ctx.Log($"wrong base: {ctx.Item.BaseName}"); break; }

    if (await ctx.CheckMods(wanted) > 0) { ctx.Log("done"); break; }
    if (!await ctx.ApplyCurrency("Orb of Scouring")) { ctx.Log("stopped early"); break; }
}
```

## When editing the plugin's own C# instead

ExileImGui only for UI. No code comments except a one-line reminder where something is genuinely
non-obvious. Few big files, sections separated by `#region`. No automated tests - the player
verifies in game. See `slop/reference/plugin-overview.md`.
